('jesus','Jesus Christ','matthew','Son and high priest whose self-offering grounds the argument about access to God','The writer connects shared suffering, enduring life, and heavenly service with him.','His work joins confidence before God with mutual care and patient endurance.',list(range(1,14))),
('moses','Moses','exodus','Faithful servant whose household care and received tent pattern support the comparisons','The writer recalls his leadership, law, received pattern, and choice of mistreatment.','His faithfulness is honored within comparisons about the Son and continued trust.',[3,7,8,9,10,11,12]),
('aaron','Aaron','exodus','Called priest whose role supplies a comparison for appointment and repeated service','The writer names his calling, priestly order, and rod within the tent.','His appointed role helps explain why priestly honor cannot be claimed for oneself.',[5,7,9]),
('melchizedek','Melchizedek','genesis','King and priest whose meeting with Abraham supports the argument about enduring priesthood','He blesses Abraham and receives a tenth of the returned goods.','The writer uses his blessing and the account\x27s silence about ancestry to explain its comparison.',[5,6,7]),
